Installation Instructions for Plymouth Theme: Arch ASCII Art
===========================================================

## AUR Installation (Recommended)

1. Install using an AUR helper:
   ```bash
   yay -S plymouth-theme-arch-ascii
   # or
   paru -S plymouth-theme-arch-ascii
   ```

2. Set the theme as default:
   ```bash
   sudo plymouth-set-default-theme arch-ascii-art
   ```

3. Update initramfs:
   ```bash
   sudo mkinitcpio -P
   ```

## Manual Installation

1. Clone the repository:
   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/tn3w/plymouth-theme-arch-ascii.git
   ```

2. Copy theme files:
   ```bash
   sudo cp -r plymouth-theme-arch-ascii /usr/share/plymouth/themes/arch-ascii-art
   ```

3. Set as default theme:
   ```bash
   sudo plymouth-set-default-theme arch-ascii-art
   ```

4. Update initramfs:
   ```bash
   sudo mkinitcpio -P
   ```

## Prerequisites

- Plymouth must be installed: `sudo pacman -S plymouth`
- For LUKS encryption support, ensure plymouth is before encrypt in mkinitcpio.conf HOOKS

## Testing

Test without rebooting:
```bash
sudo plymouthd --debug --debug-file=/tmp/plymouth-debug.log
sudo plymouth --show-splash
sudo plymouth --ask-for-password
sudo plymouth --quit
```
